title: The_End
tags:
---

Heart: You remember this place?

Mind: I think I do. It looks like my palace, my home...

Heart: That's right. And there's your crown, my friend. The throne is yours. After everything, we've made it back. 

Heart: Do you remember now?

Mind: Yeah, it does. We started here, didn’t we? Since I left the palace, Madeline's memories have been falling apart.

Mind: I have been falling apart. There were no thieves, just my own failing powers.

Heart: Case closed! I guess that means we’re at the end of our journey, huh?

Mind: Yes...yes we are.

Mind: Thank you, Heart. Your bravery led us into trouble, yet without it we could not have found each other again.

Heart: Of course! We would have never made it this far if you weren't behind me the entire time, making sure I have solid ground under my feet.

Mind: I guess I did...

Mind: ...

Mind: Heart...I'm afraid. I'm afraid that I'll forget about this crown, my pledge to protect Madeline's memories...

Mind: I'm afraid that I'll lose myself in the past once more...

Mind: I'm afraid that I'll forget you again.

Mind: ...

Heart: Hey...

Heart: It's okay...

Heart: You might forget. You might stumble. You might get lost.

Heart: Even if you forget me too, I promise you, no matter where you are, I will find you.

Mind: Even if I lock the doors? Even if I shutter the windows?

Heart: I will break every barrier to get to you. I will make a ruckus so loud that you will have to come to me.

Mind: ...

Mind: You always do...You never let me drift too far away, do you?

Heart: Because we're in this together, Mind. You guard Madeline's past, while I protect her future. We will always meet in the middle. You will always remember in the end.

Mind: ...And if I don't?

Heart: I'll be there. I'll always be there. I'll bring you home.

Heart: I'll remember for you.

<<NextScene SceneScriptHolder>>
